1
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:12,920
Try loosening up and stepping away, okay?

2
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:48,660
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out.

3
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:55,400
Walking while looking back,
led on by the clatter.

4
00:00:56,540 --> 00:01:02,640
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:07,780
So, the tiles of the arcade street

6
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:13,580
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:19,740
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:21,840
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:25,860
Politicians with their self-important faces,

10
00:01:25,860 --> 00:01:29,160
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

11
00:01:29,160 --> 00:01:34,760
Try turning at that corner.

12
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:39,980
You'll meet everyone, everyone.

13
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:47,900
There's a wall over
there surely a wall there.

14
00:01:49,120 --> 00:01:53,140
Everyone, come along to our town!

15
00:01:53,960 --> 00:01:54,720
Thank you.

16
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:59,180
Aaaah! Relentless pursuit
with unwavering aim!

17
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:09,340
Ugh.

18
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:16,220
Eeeeeeh!

19
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:17,680
Eeeeeeh!

20
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:17,880
Eeeeeeh!

21
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:18,260
Eeeeeeh!

22
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:21,020
Eeeeeeh!

23
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:22,400
Eeeeeeh!

24
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,360
Aaaaaah!

25
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:28,740
Phew, saved!

26
00:02:28,740 --> 00:02:30,560
What the...!

27
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:36,080
Where am I?

28
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:38,160
Whoa, careful!

29
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:44,800
Aaaaaaaah!

30
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:49,840
It was a dream.

31
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:50,180
A dream?

32
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:53,300
What a dream that was.

33
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:57,380
Chief, you didn't have to show up in
my dream and get angry too, did you?

34
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:06,880
Whoa! What the heck is this!

35
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,140
Don't tell me there's a
burglar at the police box?

36
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:12,080
No, I'm here,
so it can't be a burglary, can it?

37
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:15,000
Joking around isn't the time for this,
this is serious.

38
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:17,720
Nakagawa's not here either?

39
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:20,040
Reiko's not here either.

40
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:21,180
Terai! That's right!

41
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:25,440
Terai, that good-for-nothing,
how long is he going to be out on patrol?

42
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:26,940
That means...

43
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:28,980
I'm the only one at the police box.

44
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:30,620
This is going to be my responsibility...

45
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:33,660
Wait, could it be that...

46
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:36,600
Could this still be part of the dream?

47
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,600
It's not a dream after all.

48
00:03:41,460 --> 00:03:42,220
Yes, Chief.

49
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:44,540
I fell asleep during my nap,
and someone got into the empty room.

50
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:46,080
I'm sorry.

51
00:03:48,140 --> 00:03:49,900
Be careful from now on, you hear?

52
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:53,420
Like he'd ever forgive me
for saying that to the Chief!

53
00:03:53,920 --> 00:03:57,560
Uh-oh, I need to come up with a
good excuse before anyone shows up.

54
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,240
Th-Terai's back!

55
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:03,460
Nakagawa, you're early.

56
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:05,620
Nakagawa?

57
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:08,860
Reiko-san, weren't you supposed
to be out for soba today?

58
00:04:09,340 --> 00:04:11,120
I just remembered something I have to do.

59
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:13,660
Even Reiko...

60
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:15,420
Good morning.

61
00:04:16,040 --> 00:04:17,260
Whoa, what's this?

62
00:04:17,620 --> 00:04:18,600
What happened?

63
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:20,660
Just a bit of a delusion, I suppose.

64
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:27,520
In other words, while Ryo-chan was napping,

65
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:31,340
someone must have sneaked into the
police box and trashed the office

66
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:34,560
It'd be unfair to blame Ryo-san
alone after his night shift.

67
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:39,200
That's right, Terui is equally guilty for going
out on patrol and leaving the box unattended.

68
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:44,240
No, Terui's crime of leaving me behind while
I was sleeping is actually far more serious!

69
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:46,500
Ryo-chan.

70
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:53,600
But they really tore the place apart,
didn't they.

71
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:57,420
This might be harassment from
someone who holds a grudge against me.

72
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:59,760
Looks like nothing was taken, though.

73
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:01,400
That's a relief.

74
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:04,500
Still, we should report it to Chief Ohara.

75
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:08,740
Nothing was taken,
so there's no need to report it, is there?

76
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:09,620
Ryo-chan.

77
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:11,240
No, it's no use.

78
00:05:12,620 --> 00:05:12,980
It's gone.

79
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:14,640
What's gone?

80
00:05:15,860 --> 00:05:19,180
The gold badge from the Ministry of Health,
Labour and Welfare that Chief Ohara was handling.

81
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:25,300
This is the Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare badge
personally given to me by the District Headquarters Chief.

82
00:05:25,780 --> 00:05:28,600
Wow, this is real gold, isn't it?

83
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:30,140
Wanna give it a suck and see?

84
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,880
Congratulations, Chief.

85
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:36,660
Well, once you get old,
you get the occasional good thing.

86
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:41,220
Chief Ohara looked so happy.

87
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:43,740
He showed us the badge yesterday.

88
00:05:45,420 --> 00:05:46,680
He forgot it and went home.

89
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:49,680
I was supposed to hold
onto it until tomorrow.

90
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:51,400
Understood.

91
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:53,120
I'll keep it safe.

92
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,040
You definitely put it on this shelf,
didn't you?

93
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:04,800
Yeah.

94
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:06,760
Until we went out on patrol,

95
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:08,880
it was in the corner of the middle shelf.

96
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:12,000
We don't lock this shelf
during the day, right?

97
00:06:13,560 --> 00:06:15,320
Maybe it fell on the floor.

98
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:16,660
Let's look for it.

99
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:17,580
Yeah.

100
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:23,420
It's nowhere to be found! What do we do?

101
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:28,260
It was the only valuable item in this room.

102
00:06:28,260 --> 00:06:30,580
If a pro had broken into an empty room,
they wouldn't have missed it.

103
00:06:30,940 --> 00:06:32,860
What a huge blunder, Terui.

104
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:34,160
Ryo-san...

105
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:37,060
After all, it's the gold badge from the Ministry of Health,
Labour and Welfare.

106
00:06:37,060 --> 00:06:39,440
You can't buy one with money.

107
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:43,560
If it were a gold prize,
a championship, or a first-place trophy,

108
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:46,720
you might find one in the
wholesale district around Kappabashi,

109
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:49,680
but a commendation badge
is a different story.

110
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:56,140
The chief earned it after ten years of blood,
sweat, and worn-out shoe soles.

111
00:06:56,140 --> 00:06:58,220
It's a low-key award.

112
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:03,740
And you just casually left
it lying around somewhere,

113
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:07,040
so you generously handed it over to a thief.

114
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:09,440
After all, it's just a Ministry of Health,
Labour and Welfare award, right?

115
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:12,160
Ryo-chan, that's a terrible thing to say.

116
00:07:12,160 --> 00:07:13,280
That's really too much.

117
00:07:13,860 --> 00:07:17,800
You of all people, senior,
should know Terui isn't that kind of person.

118
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:20,540
I should have put it in my locker.

119
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:23,320
I hesitated for a moment back then,

120
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:28,220
but I thought that if the chief came by while I was away,
he'd spot it right away on the bookshelf.

121
00:07:29,540 --> 00:07:31,220
So it was my carelessness.

122
00:07:31,820 --> 00:07:36,220
Right, the chief's gold badge was
lost through Terui's carelessness.

123
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:39,080
We need to get this
straightened out clearly.

124
00:07:44,700 --> 00:07:45,020
What?

125
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:50,480
Is there something on my face?

126
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:52,360
Or do you like me?

127
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:56,560
Was I wrong about you, senpai?

128
00:07:58,420 --> 00:07:59,800
Don't get so worked up.

129
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:03,340
Terui and I are like the straight
man and the joker in a manzai act.

130
00:08:03,340 --> 00:08:06,340
We understand each other perfectly here,

131
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:10,308
Terui-san, don't mind what Ryo-chan said,

132
00:08:10,358 --> 00:08:12,880
let's all search for the Chief's badge.

133
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:18,960
I can't cause everyone trouble.
I'll definitely get the gold badge back

134
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:23,400
But if I don't come back,
give this to Chief Ohara

135
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,900
Master? Wait, Terui-san!

136
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:34,000
Just leave him alone,
he'll come back eventually.

137
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:36,200
Ryo-chan, Terui-san is serious this time.

138
00:08:37,040 --> 00:08:37,540
I'll go look for him.

139
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:42,080
Ow What are you doing?

140
00:08:42,660 --> 00:08:45,860
It's your fault, Ryo-chan,
for napping and not noticing the burglar.

141
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:48,940
Ow Reiko, that hurts!

142
00:08:48,940 --> 00:08:51,420
Terui-san, who's so serious,
even wrote his resignation letter!

143
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:54,140
If something happens to Terui-san,
who's so distressed...

144
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:58,440
Ryo-chan, you'll take responsibility and look
after Terui-san's wife and kids, won't you?

145
00:08:58,440 --> 00:09:01,720
Why would I have to look
after Terui's missus and brats?

146
00:09:01,720 --> 00:09:03,400
Ow

147
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:08,800
Geez, this guy's really
going all out with the hold!

148
00:09:09,180 --> 00:09:10,980
Terui's caused me no end of trouble.

149
00:09:13,980 --> 00:09:14,620
Senpai.

150
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:17,160
Terui-san isn't anywhere.

151
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:20,500
Honestly, he ran off from the
bridge with no leads at all.

152
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:24,040
How's that idiot planning
to find the culprit?

153
00:09:25,020 --> 00:09:26,480
I'll go check over that way.

154
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:30,580
Terui's actions are unassuming yet outlandish,
you know.

155
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,860
It's for the future, you see.

156
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:40,980
My kid's been begging for
something called a Kochi-Kochi Bone,

157
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:44,180
so I was going to buy it
quietly and surprise them.

158
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:46,280
It's the Flash Cam-Cam Bone, right?

159
00:09:46,280 --> 00:09:48,200
My child wants one too.

160
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:51,740
I keep telling them they have
to wait until their birthday.

161
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:55,240
I have to find a new job before then.

162
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:56,560
A new job?

163
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:00,060
Will you be all right on your own?

164
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:01,840
Yes, thank you.

165
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:06,360
To my grandchild, who always got lost
and needed looking after by Terai-san,

166
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:10,380
now they even have a child of their own.
Time really flies.

167
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:13,900
Um, well then, take care.

168
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:15,600
Oh my.

169
00:10:16,540 --> 00:10:18,720
E-excuse me, that badge.

170
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:23,340
Something wrong?

171
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:25,600
N-no, it's a nice badge.

172
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:33,120
Give me back my hat.

173
00:10:33,960 --> 00:10:34,760
Sorry.

174
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:39,380
What am I doing?

175
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:40,920
Calm down.

176
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:43,720
Calm down and think about
the culprit's movements.

177
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:48,580
Right, there must be a witness
somewhere near the police box.

178
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,940
Between 2 and 3 o'clock.

179
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:55,680
Did you see anyone suspicious
near the police box?

180
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:57,340
Suspicious person

181
00:10:58,520 --> 00:10:59,580
I woke up.

182
00:11:00,780 --> 00:11:03,480
Did you hear that? What a good boy.

183
00:11:05,780 --> 00:11:07,880
Thank you so much, you've been a big help.

184
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:10,860
Come on, say bye-bye to Terui-san.

185
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:14,420
Bye-bye!

186
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:20,040
It was around 3 o'clock, though.

187
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:22,860
Did you see anyone? A suspicious guy?

188
00:11:22,860 --> 00:11:25,940
Higher up, Terui-san.

189
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:27,460
Still higher?

190
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:29,660
Over there, further right.

191
00:11:30,580 --> 00:11:31,340
Found it!

192
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:36,320
Just a little more.

193
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:43,540
Thanks, Terui.

194
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:45,080
Anyone suspicious...

195
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:47,000
Looks like they didn't
see anything after all.

196
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:48,260
See ya.

197
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:48,760
Damn it.

198
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:49,320
Bye-bye.

199
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:55,160
Right around then I was making
deliveries near the police box.

200
00:11:55,560 --> 00:11:56,280
Really?

201
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:59,860
Yeah, a suspicious guy, a suspicious guy.

202
00:11:59,860 --> 00:12:03,860
Once you're done with that,
could you load up the rice over there too?

203
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:06,680
Sorry for making you help out, Terui.

204
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:09,340
No, even the smallest thing is fine.

205
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:11,140
If you remember anything...

206
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:20,840
Around noon, I think.

207
00:12:21,860 --> 00:12:25,140
Now that you mention it,
a man came out of the police box.

208
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:27,380
Is that right?

209
00:12:27,380 --> 00:12:30,960
If you remember anything, like what he was
wearing or his hairstyle, please tell me.

210
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:35,460
He was a bit older than you, I think.

211
00:12:35,940 --> 00:12:37,240
His hair was short.

212
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:39,020
A jacket like this one.

213
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:40,780
The kind young people wear.

214
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:44,320
Yeah, he was wearing something like that.

215
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:49,040
Thank you, that really helps. Well then.

216
00:12:49,680 --> 00:12:50,960
Whoa, Ryo-san

217
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:55,120
How do you plan to find the culprit
with just that little information?

218
00:12:56,240 --> 00:13:00,600
There are hundreds of short-haired
middle-aged men in this neighborhood alone.

219
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:03,520
Even if there are hundreds,
I'll check them one by one.

220
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,760
I won't cause you any trouble, Ryo-san.

221
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:10,540
It's already underway. They're checking the surveillance
camera footage from the dispatch office right now.

222
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:22,020
For my sake, causing everyone trouble...

223
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:24,760
You can't handle this one alone.

224
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:27,800
Honestly apologize to the
Chief and ask for forgiveness.

225
00:13:28,760 --> 00:13:29,900
What's wrong with you, Rai?

226
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:32,080
That man.

227
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:48,440
If you go off doing whatever you like and really get fired,
don't blame me.

228
00:13:52,940 --> 00:13:54,520
Why are you hiding?

229
00:13:54,520 --> 00:13:55,640
You're the one, Ryo-san.

230
00:13:57,420 --> 00:14:00,600
Excuse me, sorry to bother you,
but could I have a word?

231
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:04,940
He ran off.
He really is suspicious after all.

232
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:07,560
Really, whatever happens,
don't come crying to me.

233
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:12,480
Kei-chan

234
00:14:13,020 --> 00:14:14,740
Did the surveillance camera go back?

235
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:17,700
Yes, Terui left a little while ago.

236
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:20,740
He's nowhere to be found, senpai.

237
00:14:21,100 --> 00:14:27,980
Ryo-chan, not yet either. That's the strange part.
The surveillance device says this probably isn't the exit from the Akisu.

238
00:14:29,060 --> 00:14:31,280
Then who on earth could have done this?

239
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:41,320
Hey, wait a minute!

240
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:44,740
I said stop, so stop!

241
00:14:50,920 --> 00:14:53,160
You're really a handful, you know that?

242
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,060
Ryo-san

243
00:14:55,860 --> 00:14:56,660
What is it?

244
00:14:57,140 --> 00:14:58,740
What did I do?

245
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:01,140
Then why did you run away?

246
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:06,680
Because I'm sick of being stopped
and questioned by the police.

247
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:09,980
What happened?

248
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:11,840
If you don't mind, please tell me.

249
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:18,620
I quit my company, taking
responsibility for poor business results,

250
00:15:19,020 --> 00:15:20,420
three years ago.

251
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:22,580
and I couldn't even find another job.

252
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:25,260
I sold my house, even though
there was still a mortgage on it,

253
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:26,680
and my debts just kept
growing with interest.

254
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:28,760
I divorced a year ago,

255
00:15:28,760 --> 00:15:31,860
and sent my family back to my
wife's parents' home in Kyushu.

256
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:35,760
Since then, I've had no fixed
address and have lived from day to day.

257
00:15:37,560 --> 00:15:38,240
I haven't seen a single one of them.

258
00:15:38,780 --> 00:15:39,280
Hey.

259
00:15:41,520 --> 00:15:42,340
Ryo-san

260
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:44,840
Shiojiri-san's so pitiful.

261
00:15:44,840 --> 00:15:47,400
He's worked so hard and
honestly up till now, too.

262
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:49,000
It's just too cruel, isn't it.

263
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:51,320
What are you crying for?

264
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:54,100
I just can't see it as
someone else's problem.

265
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:57,820
I contacted Katsushika
Police Station, and...

266
00:15:57,820 --> 00:16:01,060
apparently your family has filed
a missing person report for you.

267
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:03,340
A missing person report?

268
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:04,500
Your family did?

269
00:16:05,140 --> 00:16:06,500
Shiojiri-san got divorced, so...

270
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:15,420
Well, we checked with the station, and your
wife and child are coming to pick you up.

271
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:18,660
That's right. Your wife and child

272
00:16:20,540 --> 00:16:25,380
never divorced you, Mr. Shiojiri.
She's been searching for you.

273
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:34,060
Wait quietly at the station
until your family comes for you.

274
00:16:35,260 --> 00:16:37,260
Thank you, Terui. Ryotsu.

275
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:38,820
Hang in there.

276
00:16:42,280 --> 00:16:42,960
Thank goodness.

277
00:16:42,960 --> 00:16:46,740
So the Terui matter is back to square one.

278
00:16:56,420 --> 00:16:58,520
Hey, you can't stop or park there!

279
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:01,840
A middle-aged man with short hair,
wearing a jacket.

280
00:17:03,260 --> 00:17:04,060
Terui!

281
00:17:04,060 --> 00:17:05,560
Hey, Terui!

282
00:17:30,660 --> 00:17:31,580
Aaaaaah!

283
00:17:31,580 --> 00:17:32,540
Aaaaaah!

284
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:33,400
Aaaaaah!

285
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:37,680
How dare you pull that stunt on me!

286
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:38,860
Aaaaaah!

287
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:40,780
Just look at this!

288
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:42,040
Aaaaaah!

289
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:47,240
All talk, these guys have no substance.

290
00:17:48,380 --> 00:17:50,400
Yikes! We're filming live!

291
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:53,240
Officer, you can't interfere with our shoot!

292
00:17:55,280 --> 00:17:58,060
Well Ryo-san, let's return that sword.

293
00:18:00,440 --> 00:18:02,200
Phew, that startled me.

294
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:06,020
If it was a movie shoot,
I'd have wanted to appear in proper costume.

295
00:18:06,020 --> 00:18:08,540
That man from before.

296
00:18:12,620 --> 00:18:13,700
So he's an actor

297
00:18:19,760 --> 00:18:21,020
Hey, wait a minute.

298
00:18:21,620 --> 00:18:23,200
Excuse me.

299
00:18:23,920 --> 00:18:25,100
Yes, what's the matter?

300
00:18:30,340 --> 00:18:34,660
Sorry about the mess,
I think it'll be tidied up soon.

301
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:40,480
About that, actually, our Marie and John -

302
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:50,240
No, Marie, come here right now!

303
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:58,140
What should I do?

304
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:03,260
So it was the dog that
ransacked the police box?

305
00:19:03,260 --> 00:19:04,820
I'm so sorry.

306
00:19:04,820 --> 00:19:10,440
I can't find the gold badge in the black
case that was on the bookshelf over there.

307
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:12,560
Do you know anything about it?

308
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:16,660
Well, we didn't take anything out, though.

309
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:20,120
Anyway, I should let Terui-san know.

310
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:29,500
Damn, what a persistent guy.

311
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:39,640
What?

312
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:48,540
Don't let him get away!

313
00:19:48,840 --> 00:19:49,920
Hey, let go!

314
00:19:50,340 --> 00:19:50,840
No way!

315
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:52,260
Let's just talk, shall we!

316
00:19:52,960 --> 00:19:54,320
Let go, I said let go!

317
00:19:58,100 --> 00:19:59,520
You're so damn annoying!

318
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,260
Ryo-san...

319
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:22,080
Personal belongings of actors and extras,
stolen from that film set earlier

320
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:23,480
I found them.

321
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:24,380
As if that's possible.

322
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:31,400
Terui, this guy is a habitual bag-snatcher.

323
00:20:31,780 --> 00:20:34,520
Looks like we've finally
hit the real target.

324
00:20:36,260 --> 00:20:39,140
It's no good, Ryo-san.
The Chief's gold badge isn't here.

325
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:43,700
Didn't you break into the
police box around noon today?

326
00:20:43,700 --> 00:20:44,720
Police box?

327
00:20:46,660 --> 00:20:48,420
Breaking into a place like that,
what were you planning to steal?

328
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:49,480
A helmet?

329
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:50,940
A duralumin shield?

330
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:53,380
That's enough already.

331
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:54,480
Ryo-san.

332
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:55,400
Thank you.

333
00:20:56,180 --> 00:20:57,380
Don't apologize, Terui.

334
00:21:01,740 --> 00:21:03,780
We caught a habitual thief.

335
00:21:04,480 --> 00:21:06,060
The Chief will surely

336
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:07,580
overlook the badge matter, right?

337
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:12,580
Ryo-san was the one who caught him.

338
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:13,680
Besides,

339
00:21:14,380 --> 00:21:15,760
making a deal like that,

340
00:21:16,660 --> 00:21:17,620
I can't do that.

341
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:22,540
We've had our share of
trouble with Ryo-san until now,

342
00:21:23,180 --> 00:21:24,040
but today's events

343
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:27,260
I won't forget for the rest of my life,
even if I quit the police force.

344
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:30,160
Terui!

345
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,400
It's you two.

346
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:35,660
Ah!

347
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:37,460
Chief!

348
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:40,520
I happened to be passing by,

349
00:21:40,980 --> 00:21:43,500
and I heard men were brawling in the grass.

350
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:45,880
So I came to see what was going on.

351
00:21:50,080 --> 00:21:57,100
Beep-beep. Well, what happened to that? This?
I tried going a little younger. How does it look?

352
00:21:57,100 --> 00:22:04,240
A gold badge Ah, I suddenly have to meet
a friend from my student days tonight.

353
00:22:04,780 --> 00:22:13,440
Might as well show it off, I figured. I went back to the
police box to get it around noon. Hadn't you told Ryo yet?

354
00:22:13,440 --> 00:22:15,700
I told you, didn't I?

355
00:22:15,700 --> 00:22:18,920
Ryo-san, what's going on?

356
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:21,040
W-well then,

357
00:22:26,260 --> 00:22:29,480
Hey, Ryotsu! Don't sleep on duty.

358
00:22:31,060 --> 00:22:33,240
Come on, Chief. I'm not sleeping.

359
00:22:34,840 --> 00:22:39,740
Tell Terui I went back
for the gold badge, got it?

360
00:22:39,740 --> 00:22:41,200
Understood.

361
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:45,960
Argh! Don't you dare fall asleep!
"I'm not sleeping,"

362
00:22:45,960 --> 00:22:46,840
Coming in!

363
00:22:46,840 --> 00:22:48,300
Eeeeeh?

364
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:50,480
Aaaaaah!

365
00:23:05,680 --> 00:23:07,520
So that wasn't a dream after all?

366
00:23:08,840 --> 00:23:11,480
So you knew everything, Ryo-san.

367
00:23:12,220 --> 00:23:15,080
Well, to be precise,
that's not quite right, Terui.

368
00:23:15,080 --> 00:23:18,440
I was half-asleep back then,
so I barely had any awareness.

369
00:23:21,020 --> 00:23:25,080
What's with that look? We just
confirmed our friendship a moment ago!

370
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:32,860
Calm down.
Isn't it good that the gold badge was found?

371
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,700
The Chief is here too.

372
00:23:37,860 --> 00:23:39,600
What's the matter with all of you?

373
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:42,400
So the gold badge was found?

374
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:43,780
I'm so glad.

375
00:23:43,780 --> 00:23:46,800
It was here all along

376
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:48,960
Ryo-san, you knew, didn't you?

377
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:50,480
You did, didn't you?

378
00:23:51,020 --> 00:23:51,980
Ryo-san!

379
00:23:53,720 --> 00:23:56,000
Somehow,
you're different from your usual Terui.

380
00:24:23,320 --> 00:24:25,960
Your demands are only reasonable.

381
00:24:27,120 --> 00:24:30,660
But I'm getting by with just one hand,

382
00:24:30,660 --> 00:24:33,400
a beef bowl with extra soupy sauce,

383
00:24:33,980 --> 00:24:36,760
and the frustration of endless overtime,

384
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:40,340
all cleared away by getting irritated.

385
00:24:43,680 --> 00:24:46,460
Every day is no problem.

386
00:24:46,460 --> 00:24:50,140
After passing through a hot shower,

387
00:24:50,140 --> 00:24:56,720
every day is no problem-brain,
energy restored by a sleep pillow.

388
00:24:59,860 --> 00:25:06,340
Every day is no problem-brain.
I love someone like me.

389
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:13,100
Every day is no problem-brain.
A Monday with hearts flying around.

390
00:25:13,100 --> 00:25:17,000
Spin step, spin step, pro blend.

391
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:20,840
Over there is Kameary.

392
00:25:21,980 --> 00:25:24,180
Surely it's Kameary.

393
00:25:25,360 --> 00:25:29,180
Everyone, come on over to our town.

394
00:25:30,360 --> 00:25:30,840
Thank you.

